{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AXVupHww5uFbCztsPFLZ5s","type":"tool_result","content":"961:                                  |    [waypoint] per-NS  L7 (Envoy)\n996:[Omitted long matching line]\n1089:A) Ambient mode uses a per-node L4 proxy and optional per-namespace L7 proxies, and the L7 waypoint is a deployment of Envoy — the same engine sidecar mode uses\n1129:**5. A.** In ambient mode \"Istio implements its features using a per-node Layer 4 (L4) proxy, and optionally a per-namespace Layer 7 (L7) proxy,\" and the waypoint proxy \"is a deployment of the Envoy proxy; the same engine that Istio uses for its sidecar data plane mode\" [source: istio-ambient-mode-2026-08-31].\n1131:- **B is wrong** on the key detail, and it is the near-miss worth understanding. Ambient does add a purpose-built proxy, ztunnel, at L4, per node, but the L7 waypoint is Envoy. Ambient removes *sidecars*, not Envoy.\n1755:| \"Service mesh means sidecars\" | Sidecar mode puts an Envoy proxy beside each Pod; ambient mode uses per-node L4 proxies plus optional per-namespace Envoy waypoints. Both use Envoy. |\n1864:B) It uses a per-node L4 proxy called ztunnel, with optional per-namespace L7 waypoint proxies that are deployments of Envoy\n1968:[Omitted long matching line]\n2013:| **Sidecar vs ambient** | Sidecar: an Envoy per Pod. Ambient: per-node ztunnel at L4, optional per-namespace Envoy waypoints at L7. **Both use Envoy.** They coexist. |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1bcd220-900e-4c7a-8860-3284f1f082f9","uuid":"327d872d-78a4-4730-8cae-ec8221184e4c","timestamp":"2026-08-31T23:40:08.531Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"961:                                  |    [waypoint] per-NS  L7 (Envoy)\n996:[Omitted long matching line]\n1089:A) Ambient mode uses a per-node L4 proxy and optional per-namespace L7 proxies, and the L7 waypoint is a deployment of Envoy — the same engine sidecar mode uses\n1129:**5. A.** In ambient mode \"Istio implements its features using a per-node Layer 4 (L4) proxy, and optionally a per-namespace Layer 7 (L7) proxy,\" and the waypoint proxy \"is a deployment of the Envoy proxy; the same engine that Istio uses for its sidecar data plane mode\" [source: istio-ambient-mode-2026-08-31].\n1131:- **B is wrong** on the key detail, and it is the near-miss worth understanding. Ambient does add a purpose-built proxy, ztunnel, at L4, per node, but the L7 waypoint is Envoy. Ambient removes *sidecars*, not Envoy.\n1755:| \"Service mesh means sidecars\" | Sidecar mode puts an Envoy proxy beside each Pod; ambient mode uses per-node L4 proxies plus optional per-namespace Envoy waypoints. Both use Envoy. |\n1864:B) It uses a per-node L4 proxy called ztunnel, with optional per-namespace L7 waypoint proxies that are deployments of Envoy\n1968:[Omitted long matching line]\n2013:| **Sidecar vs ambient** | Sidecar: an Envoy per Pod. Ambient: per-node ztunnel at L4, optional per-namespace Envoy waypoints at L7. **Both use Envoy.** They coexist. |","numLines":9,"totalLines":9}}
